{
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "autoloader-generic",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "The app ships no composer/autoload.php, so the server registers its generic loader for lib/ and looks every class up in the file system.",
        "  A composer/composer.json with config.vendor-dir \".\", config.optimize-autoloader true, a config.autoloader-suffix and autoload.psr-4 {\"OCA\\\\Pexip\\\\\": \"../lib/\"} makes composer dump-autoload write composer/autoload.php with a class map; the code of the app does not change."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "route-unreferenced",
      "level": "warn",
      "places": [
        "PUT /index.php/apps/integration_pexip/config  integration_pexip.config.setconfig  appinfo/routes.php:11 routes",
        "GET /index.php/apps/integration_pexip/policy/v1/service/configuration  integration_pexip.pexipapi.checkcall  appinfo/routes.php:13 routes"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "Nothing in the app calls 2 routes outside OCS. Looked for: a route name or a path in the PHP source and the templates, in 8 files of the frontend source and in the navigation of info.xml. The frontend puts the path of the app and the rest of a URL together at run time, so every text there that reads like a path below the app counted as a call. A route stays behind when the frontend stops calling it. A route that only a client outside the app calls shows here as well, unless its method allows requests from other origins (CORS).",
        "  PUT /index.php/apps/integration_pexip/config  integration_pexip.config.setconfig  appinfo/routes.php:11 routes",
        "  GET /index.php/apps/integration_pexip/policy/v1/service/configuration  integration_pexip.pexipapi.checkcall  appinfo/routes.php:13 routes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "dev-tools-in-root",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [],
      "lines": [
        "phpunit/phpunit is in require-dev of composer.json. The manual recommends a vendor-bin/ of bamarni/composer-bin-plugin per tool, so that the dependencies of a tool cannot conflict with those of the app."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "job-time-sensitivity",
      "level": "info",
      "places": [
        "lib/Cron/CleanupCalls.php OCA\\Pexip\\Cron\\CleanupCalls"
      ],
      "lines": [
        "1 timed job does not say whether it is time sensitive. A job that sets TIME_INSENSITIVE with setTimeSensitivity() is moved to the maintenance window of the server; whether a job is heavy enough for that only its maintainer knows.",
        "  lib/Cron/CleanupCalls.php OCA\\Pexip\\Cron\\CleanupCalls"
      ]
    },
